<title>BRAZIL: Trading in Brazil's Copel suspended - bolsa.</title>
<headline>Trading in Brazil's Copel suspended - bolsa.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in shares of Brazilian electrical power firm Copel was suspended Monday because the details of a shareholders' meeting on Friday were not disclosed to the market, a Sao Paulo bourse spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The spokeswoman described the suspension as a &quot;normal procedure,&quot; adding that trading would resume as soon as the bourse received a report on what was discussed at the meeting.</p>
<p>Copel, known formally as Companhia Paranaense de Energia, is a power distribution firm owned by the southeastern Brazilian state of Parana.</p>
<p>((--James Craig, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 248 5413))</p>
